<%#
    Two faces, and only two.

    Fraunces sets everything the eye reads as a title or a quantity — page
    headings, the figures in the ledger, the counts along the verification
    chain — and Inter everything read as an instruction. That division is the
    whole typographic idea: a register, not a dashboard.

    Fraunces is a variable font, so the optical-size axis comes along with the
    weights and a 44px heading is drawn with finer detail than a 15px one
    without a second file. The italic is asked for because the eyebrow above
    every page title and the "anniversary" mark in the almanac are set in it.
%>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,400;0,9..144,500;0,9..144,600;1,9..144,400;1,9..144,500&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
